# Marketing website build-time configuration.
#
# Astro inlines PUBLIC_* variables at BUILD time, so these must be present when
# `npm run build` runs — including inside the Docker build on the server, where
# docker-compose passes them through as build args (see docker-compose.yml).
#
# Leave PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY empty to disable analytics entirely: the site then
# ships with no PostHog code path at all, which is the correct local-dev default.

# PostHog project API key ("Project API Key" in Project settings — the public
# phc_… one, NOT a personal API key).
PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=

# The PostHog host the browser talks to.
#
# Production points this at a first-party relay on our own origin rather than
# straight at PostHog: ad blockers drop 10-25% of events sent to the vendor's
# domain, which at this site's volume is the difference between seeing a visit
# and not. The relay lives in the xdevapp-infra repo, in the sonoqui.pro block
# of caddy/sites.d/sonoqui.caddy — /relay/static/* goes to the assets host and
# everything else to the ingest host. Data still lands on PostHog's EU cloud in
# Frankfurt either way; only the browser's first hop changes.
#
# The prefix is /relay rather than the conventional /ingest because several
# blocklists match /ingest by name, which would defeat the point.
#
#   production: https://sonoqui.pro/relay
#   local dev:  https://eu.i.posthog.com   (nothing is proxying a dev server)
PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://eu.i.posthog.com
